Screens of the two agents the built-in tmux wake reads before typing (`mail::pane_state`).

Captured from real sessions, one file per state:

    idle              an empty input box (claude: with its suggestion; `idle-after-turn`: without)
    typing            text typed at the box, not sent
    working           a turn in progress, box empty (`working-tool`: a tool running)
    working-typed     a turn in progress, text typed at the box
    question          the agent asked a question (claude AskUserQuestion, agy ask_question)
    permission        a shell command waiting for approval
    menu              the folder-trust dialog shown on first start in a directory
    narrow-working    claude, a turn with its spinner in a narrow pane; the footer is cut to `esc to i…`
    narrow-working-streaming  claude, the reply streaming with no spinner line; only the cut footer shows it
    narrow-idle       claude, an empty box with a faint suggestion in a narrow pane; the footer is cut to `← for ag…`

The `claude-325-` ones are Claude Code 2.1.325, which draws no `esc to interrupt` and lists its
background agents under the mode line:

    325-idle          an empty box, with its suggestion
    325-working       a turn in progress, box empty; the spinner line is above the box
    325-transcript    the ctrl+o transcript view: no box, `Showing detailed transcript` on the last line
    325-narrow-transcript  the same at 52 columns; the footer is cut to `ctrl+o to to…verbose`
    325-agents2-idle  two background agents running, the turn over
    325-agents3-working  three background agents running and a turn in progress: more rows
                      under the box than `MAX_LINES_BELOW_INPUT` allows without the list left out
    325-agents3-idle  three background agents running, the turn over
    325-narrow-agents3-idle  the same at 52 columns
    325-idle-quotes-footer   the turn over, its reply a line that says `esc to interrupt`
    325-idle-quotes-spinner  the turn over, its reply quoting a spinner line (`✻ Pondering… (6s ·
                      thinking)`), one at column 0 behind `⏺` and one indented under it
    325-working-queued  a turn in progress with a message queued (typed and sent meanwhile); queued
                      messages are drawn at column 0 above the spinner, the box shows `Press up to
                      edit queued messages` faint
    325-working-todos  a turn in progress with a task list (started with
                      `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TASKS=1 CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TODO_TOOLS=1`); the list is
                      drawn indented under the spinner, which stays at column 0

The three `narrow-` ones: Claude Code 2.1.300 at 52x30, fullscreen UI, started with
`-n adjutant-read-<name> --permission-mode dontAsk`, so the session name is drawn in the box's
top border and the footer is cut to the width.

Versions: Claude Code 2.1.284, Antigravity CLI (agy) 1.2.6, tmux 3.7c. Each ran in its own
pane of 100x30 on an isolated tmux server, driven with `send-keys`. The `claude-325-` ones:
Claude Code 2.1.325, tmux 3.8, 100x30 and (`narrow`) 52x30, the same way, but started without
`-n`, so the box's top border has no name in it.

Format: what `tmux_capture_script` prints. The screen, from `capture-pane -p -e -J`; a line
`@@adjutant:pane@@`; then `pane_in_mode`, `cursor_x` and `cursor_y` separated by tabs.

Editing applied, since the repository is public: the escape sequences were dropped from every
line except claude's input line (its suggestion is told from typed text by being faint; a
test puts escapes back on every line to check nothing else depends on them; a few other lines
still carry theirs, such as the OSC 8 link in claude-menu.txt and the `❯` line in
claude-working.txt); the account, plan
and working directory were replaced with placeholders; a custom status line, spinner wording
and question text were replaced with plain English; trailing spaces were trimmed. In the
`claude-325-` ones the status line (which carried usage figures), the replies, the token counts
of the agent rows and the tip about the terminal's own configuration were replaced or dropped;
the rows, blanks and borders stay where they were drawn. In the four that quote or queue, the
spinner wording (a custom one) and the replies that were not about the point were replaced with
plain English or the placeholder line; what the prompts and quotes say is as sent.

When an agent release changes how it draws these, capture the screen again the same way
rather than editing the files by hand.
